  "conclusions": [
    "Compact-field compression is not the causal SPIn unary bottleneck on the Lego/Room sentinels. Compact preserves exact-capability primitive ranking closely and does not regress rendered unary in the two-scene macro.",
    "The unsafe base design is adaptor-after-fused-raw-MPR. Its primitive probability standard deviation collapses from 0.04714 to 0.000233, roughly 202 times smaller, and reference-only IoU loses 0.31920 macro versus capability-before-MPR.",
    "Official DINOv3/SAM3 capability projection must remain before MPR, or the compact field must be explicitly capability-supervised as the current field is. A single fused raw center is not a sufficient statistic for nonlinear adaptor capabilities.",
    "Lego also exposes a calibration issue: exact and compact both move from about 0.29 fixed IoU to about 0.60 with a reference-only threshold while retaining nearly identical ranking. This is an interface calibration effect, not compression loss.",
    "Because exact capability does not beat compact, widening the persistent field or replacing it with uncompressed capability MPR is not justified by this ladder. Remaining strict-SPIn work should target source observation/completion and reference-derived probability calibration; compatible target-RGB SAM remains a separately labelled track."
